course: dictionary
lesson: 4299
title: One word, many moods
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. The word grim can mean serious, bad, gloomy or horrible. Look at the words around it to decide. «Toad is dragged off in chains, shrieking, across the market-place... into a grim old castle» is about a dark, scary place, so grim means gloomy there.
explain: Grim can also describe a face. «A grim face» means a serious, stern face with no smile. If the news is grim, it is bad and worrying. The clues are always in the sentence: a face, a place, news or a feeling.
explain: Britons also use grim in everyday talk. In the sentence «The school toilets were grim», grim means horrible or disgusting. Nobody is saying the toilets are serious or gloomy. Saying «that's grim» is like saying «yuck».
fact: Grim means very serious, stern and unsmiling, as in «a grim face».
fact: Grim means unpleasant, worrying or sad, as in «grim news».
fact: A grim place is dark, cold and gloomy.
fact: In UK informal talk, grim means horrible or disgusting.
fact: «Hold on like grim death» means to hold very tightly.
exercise: «The old man had a grim face and never smiled.» What does grim mean here? | *Very serious and stern | Very quick | Very funny | Very wet
exercise: «The news from the flood zone was grim.» What kind of news was it? | Long and funny | *Bad, worrying and sad | Good and exciting | Quiet and soft
exercise: Find and copy one word that means dark, cold and gloomy: «The grim old castle stood on the cliff.» | *grim | stood | cliff | castle
test: Ruby says «The school toilets were grim» means they were nice and clean. What does grim mean here? | Very loud | *Horrible or disgusting | Shiny and new | Friendly
test: «He held on to the rope like grim death.» What does this mean? | Let go quickly | Sing loudly | *Hold very tightly | Fall down
exam: Why does Toad's journey feel frightening in «into a grim old castle, up winding stairs, past soldiers and guard-dogs»? | Everyone is laughing and singing | *The place is dark, cold and gloomy, with soldiers and guard-dogs | Toad is going home for tea | A picnic is being held there
